@startuml autonomous-offering-relationships
title Autonomous Offering Canonical Relationships ; per CR-ES-019 section 7

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "Autonomous Offering" as AO

class "Offering" as O
class "Authority" as Auth
class "Policy" as Pol
class "Constraint" as Con
class "Objective" as Obj
class "Context" as Ctx
class "Outcome" as Out
class "Workflow" as Wf
class "Agentic Workflow" as AWf
class "Autonomous Operations" as AOp
class "Capability" as Cap
class "Product" as P
class "Service" as S
class "Value" as V

AO --|> O : specializes
AO --> Auth : operates-within
AO --> Pol : governed-by
AO --> Con : constrained-by
AO --> Obj : pursues
AO --> Ctx : responds-to
AO --> Out : produces
AO --> Ctx : adapts-to
AO --> Wf : uses
AO --> AWf : uses
AO --> AOp : supported-by
AO --> Cap : supports
AO --> P : uses
AO --> S : uses
AO --> V : contributes-to

note bottom of AO
  No foundational concept silently introduced per CR-ES-019 section 7.
  Foundational Dependency Gate documented per ADR-ES-019 section 2.
  Deferred concepts per ADR-ES-019 section 18.
end note

@enduml
